 "pdf": "ads8361.pdf",
 "pages": "p.2 (ROC), p.3-4 (specs: tCONV 1.6 us at 10 MHz, BVDD ranges, twos complement), p.5 (truth table), p.6 (pinouts, pin descriptions), p.7 (timing: t9 30 ns), p.12-13 (Figure 8 codes, Table II, Table III), p.14 (modes II-IV, reading data)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs and the internal 2.5 V reference (REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V differential code 0000h",
  "the serial frame is synchronized by the RD pulse; the model uses RD as an active-low chip select, so a frame starts when the RD high pulse ends (the datasheet: data valid on the CLOCK falling edges after RD's rising edge, first bit after the third rising CLOCK edge) and ends at the next RD pulse; CS (output enable / tri-state of both serial outputs, and enable of CONVST and RD) is not modeled, keep it low",
  "CLOCK is a continuous conversion clock (20 clocks per conversion, fCLK 0.1-10 MHz); the conversion is timed at 1.6 us (fCLK = 10 MHz) instead of being counted in clocks; BUSY falls after the third LSB is transmitted, which the model approximates by the conversion time",
  "SERIAL DATA B (converter B in modes I and III) is never driven; SERIAL DATA A always shows converter A's 20-bit word (CH0/1 flag, CHA/B flag, D15-D0, two zeros), and with M1 = 1 (modes II/IV) both words, A then B (CHA/B flag 0 then 1), 40 clocks",
  "four-channel mode (M0 = 1): the alternating channel sequence and the CH0/1 flag (0/1) are not modeled (the flag is always 0); A0 latching on the first CLOCK falling edge selects channel 0/1 but does not change the 0 V result; the second CONVST ignored when M1 = 1",
  "pipeline: the serial output carries the previous conversion's result on the part; the 0 V code is constant",
  "tFloat: no tri-state delay is specified; tF/tR output edge times (25/30 ns) are not modeled"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS8361 only; the ADS8363/ADS7263/ADS7223 (ads7223.pdf) are the register-programmable successors with the same RD/CONVST/CLOCK interface",
